  "reason": "Evidence: config_022 (multimodal, PCA n2000 + ViT-L, concat, single profile) is the best result so far at 0.535 accuracy, outperforming RNA alone (0.485) and image alone (~0.22). However, we have only tested one fusion strategy (concat). Uncertainty: whether weighted fusion could further improve upon concat by allowing the model to learn modality-specific importance weights, especially given that the image modality alone is very weak (~0.22) and may be adding noise through a simple concatenation. This experiment (config_023) is a clean A/B test against config_022, changing only the fusion method from concat to weighted while holding all other factors constant (same encoders, same profile setting). It is the best use of the next budget slot because it reduces uncertainty about a critical design choice with zero confounding, and the result directly informs whether all subsequent multimodal experiments should use weighted or concat fusion."
}

